person/musa-ibn-abi-al-afiya | Musa ibn Abi al-Afiya al-Miknasi, the greatest king of his branch; first an Idrisid client holding Tahert and the Middle Maghreb, then he proclaimed Ubaydallah al-Mahdi's da'wa, expelled Yahya ibn Idris from Fez and ruled the Maghreb for Qayrawan, beat the Idrisid al-Hajjam at Wadi al-Matahin between Taza and Fez — until the eunuch Maysur marched in 323 and exiled him to the Malwiyya desert; he returned, besieged Nekour, and remained chief of Miknasa as a Zirid client until the Almoravids destroyed his house.
