person/musa-ibn-rahhu | Musa ibn Rahhu ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Haqq al-Marini; he joined the Ghumara hills in the princes' revolt against Sultan Abu Yusuf, then crossed to al-Andalus in 670 AH where Ibn al-Ahmar appointed him over all the ghazi-mujahidin there as their elder and spokesman — thus founding the Banu Rahhu leadership over the Andalus ghazis, inherited by his brother Abd al-Haqq then his son Hammu.
